<spell-notebook "select theming">
	<header level="1">
		Select
		<header>A select lets a user choose a value from a list, with the platform's own picker.</>
	</>
	<select-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-select-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a form, `:root`), or on
			the select's box through `::part(select)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through
			a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. Style the rest with `::part()`: `button`, `option`,
			`placeholder` and `group`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-select {
			  --ui-select-radius: 0;
			}
			ui-select::part(option) {
			  padding-block: 0.75em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				The open picker is styled only where the browser has the customizable select; elsewhere `option` and `group`
				reach as far as the platform's list lets them. Never set the `--_ui-select-*` names: they're the sheet's
				private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-select" playground>
				<ui-select placeholder="Gender" name="gender">
					<ui-item value="male">Male</>
					<ui-item value="female">Female</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
